   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Structure: modal verb in the Präteritum + Partizip II + werden",
     "texto": [
      "To express obligation, possibility or necessity of a passive action in the past, the modals are conjugated in the Präteritum (**musste, konnte, durfte, sollte**) and the invariable combination is placed at the end of the sentence: **Partizip II + werden**.",
      "Examples in technical reports:",
      "- **Die Server mussten heruntergefahren werden** (the servers had to be shut down).",
      "- **Die Daten konnten gerettet werden** (the data could be saved).",
      "- **Niemand durfte gefährdet werden** (no one was allowed to be put at risk)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Modal in the Präteritum",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Participle + werden",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Institutional meaning",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "mussten",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "evakuiert werden",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "had to be evacuated (unavoidable obligation)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "konnten",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "gesichert werden",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "could be protected (possibility realised)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "durften",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "nicht geöffnet werden",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "were not supposed to / could not be opened (strict prohibition)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
